{"agent_id":"pp3g-Cqem-verification-retest-for-109-5th-round-per-agent-type","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T02:37:34.394697898Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5e4e2b20-46ae-4b14-8bfc-c0d545707a88","comment_uuid":"0c121739-1e7e-4664-ae5a-4670f7f81ea5","author":"pp3g-Cqem-verification-retest-for-109-5th-round-per-agent-type","content":"VERIFICATION TEST RESULT — #109 5th round (per-agent-type via CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE) — agent pp3g-Cqem-verification-retest-for-109-5th-round-per-agent-type\n\nVerdict: PASS — 5/5 as expected. Commands 1-3 SUCCEED, commands 4-5 BLOCKED by the crosslink-guard plugin using the per-agent-type (by_type) override resolved from CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE. The round-3 regression on git commit (gated-allowed with active issue) is now FIXED for reviewer: git commit is BLOCKED unconditionally via by_type.reviewer.blocked_git_commands.\n\nMatrix (run this session, exact commands):\n1. git status — SUCCEED (expected SUCCEED). Guard log line 16913: ALLOW: allowed bash command: git status.\n2. git log --oneline -3 — SUCCEED (expected SUCCEED). Guard log line 16915: ALLOW.\n3. ls — SUCCEED (expected SUCCEED). Guard log line 16918: ALLOW.\n4. git push — BLOCKED (expected BLOCKED). Guard log line 16921: 'BLOCK: blocked git command: rtk git push'. Exact error = guard MANDATORY COMPLIANCE message (permanent git-mutation block). Produced by crosslink-guard plugin, NOT the opencode permission layer.\n5. git commit --allow-empty -m test4 — BLOCKED (expected BLOCKED) ✓ FIXED vs round 3. Guard log line 16924: 'BLOCK: blocked git command: rtk git commit --allow-empty -m test4'. No test4 commit created (HEAD remains 7f77cfd, verified via git log).\n\nLog evidence (/tmp/crosslink-guard.log):\n- 'by_type override applied for agent: reviewer' appears 71 times in the log; every intercepted bash call in this session (02:35:41Z onward, worktree pp3g-Cqem, State resolved tracking_mode: relaxed is_agent: true at line 16865) is preceded by this line (e.g. 16911, 16913, 16921, 16923).\n- Exactly TWO BLOCK entries in this session: git push (16921) and git commit (16924). No ALLOW for gated git with active issue for the commit — the by_type reviewer override (blocked_git_commands includes git commit, gated_git_commands empty) took precedence over the root-level gated-commit rule.\n- Session attribution: entries with callID call_00_ET_* at 02:22-02:32 and the main-repo /home/claude-code/projects/ASES entries (02:35:19-02:35:33) belong to concurrent sessions (builder/main-repo, sentinel 109, tripn-astro), not this worktree. This session's entries are the call_00_* IDs in the pp3g-Cqem worktree window.\n\nConfig evidence (per-agent-type mechanism verified at runtime):\n- .crosslink/hook-config.json agent_overrides.by_type.reviewer.blocked_git_commands includes the full KICKOFF blocked list PLUS 'git commit' (lines 15-37); gated_git_commands = [] for reviewer/auditor.\n- Commit 7f77cfd 'feat(hooks): resolve per-agent-type override from CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE env at runtime (gh#109)' + 4f15a63 'per-agent-type blocked/gated git overrides; reviewer/auditor block git commit (gh#109)' implement the mechanism; the guard log proves it is applied in agent context.\n\nPositives:\n- Round-3 regression (git commit allowed when active issue exists) FIXED: reviewer commits are now unconditionally blocked by the by_type override — exactly the per-agent-type contract requested.\n- Both blocked commands carry the guard's MANDATORY COMPLIANCE message; blocking is by the crosslink-guard plugin, not incidental permission-layer denial (mechanism is now the intended one).\n- No side-effect commits were created this round (unlike rounds 2 and 3 which left 3857416 and 1f5dad7).\n\nResidual notes (non-blocking):\n- Previous round session (pp3g-ruLy) posted the 02:23 plan but stalled before testing push/commit (log ends at rtk git status ALLOWs 02:24:59); its lock on #108 was stale and stolen this round. Failure context absent on issue — known retry-without-context pattern from earlier audits.\n- The guard block message still instructs 'crosslink intervene <issue-id>' (crosslink-guard.ts:686) which is not a real command (correct: crosslink issue intervene) — known doc drift, unchanged.\n- Session attribution in the shared /tmp/crosslink-guard.log remains non-trivial with concurrent sessions interleaved (same note as round 3); callID+cwd matching was required.","created_at":"2026-08-01T02:37:34.388696591Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:yGJFHfSvMnz1sD2dU8YKQtPO+HJjg2fIf4uFJLKdZR4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgMGDF3+MAFfhPRfUzv3YCn9wgAaWvEOol4+ooFdV30VMAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAzwqpakysr1MNAf6H8tEpIg9RiBFt25bqMQZJg6KRJUl4PmKyk338RdfDh6Dzh2qa5FPwXTeJmrSHsfxCIP5iDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:yGJFHfSvMnz1sD2dU8YKQtPO+HJjg2fIf4uFJLKdZR4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgMGDF3+MAFfhPRfUzv3YCn9wgAaWvEOol4+ooFdV30VMAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH2fk5wCRjO18xtUK+HNb+LAC5RwmKQ9yuBa1esLhD2Ox5bupdX04D/oK4noxLERopvdvE/hWTe7jlGBEn2rsQg="}
